            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Education</strong><br>\nLudwig von Mises was born on September 29, 1881, in Lemberg, in the Austro-Hungarian Empire. He was a prominent figure in the Austrian School of economic thought and was known for his work on praxeology, a study of human choice and action.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise as an Economist</strong><br>\nVon Mises established himself with his 1912 book \"The Theory of Money and Credit,\" which was one of the first to integrate monetary theory with economic theory. His work extended to cover various economic topics, including socialism and bureaucracy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Opposition to Socialism and Interventionism</strong><br>\nMises was a staunch critic of socialism and government intervention. He argued that socialism was impractical because it lacked a means to allocate resources efficiently without a price system driven by the free market.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Emigration and Impact in the United States</strong><br>\nAfter fleeing the Nazis, von Mises emigrated to the United States in 1940. He became a visiting professor at New York University and continued to write prolifically, influencing generations of economists.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy in Economic Thought</strong><br>\nMises's work has had a lasting impact on economic theory, particularly through his criticism of central planning and his advocacy for laissez-faire capitalism. He believed that only a free-market economy could facilitate true economic calculation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Key Contributions</strong><br>\nHis contributions to economics include his business cycle theory, which posits that credit expansion by banks creates unsustainable economic booms, leading inevitably to busts.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
